Signal is extending screenshot-blocking protections to iPhones and supported Android devices to prevent AI assistants such as <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> and Gemini from capturing private conversations.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/11/signal-logo.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-921884" /><br/>
In its <a href="https://signal.org/blog/protecting-your-privacy/">announcement</a>, Signal said AI assistants can capture messages displayed on screen, potentially exposing conversations to processing outside the app. End-to-end encryption protects message delivery, but cannot prevent another app from reading messages visible on a recipient's device.<br/>
<br/>
On iPhones running <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, the new "Block &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI" setting is enabled by default in Signal version 8.37 or later. It blocks screenshots, screen recordings, and AI screen-reading. On supported Android devices running Signal 8.35.1 or later, screen security activates when an AI assistant attempts to read the screen.<br/>
<br/>
iPhone users can disable the protection under Signal's <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>Privacy</strong> → <strong>Block Siri AI</strong>, either permanently or for 10 minutes to take a screenshot. Apple also offers an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/how-to/stop-siri-search-accessing-iphone-apps/">Excluded Apps setting</a> under <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>Siri</strong> that prevents &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; from accessing selected apps.<br/>
<br/>
Signal previously blocked Microsoft's Recall from capturing chats on Windows 11. It said equivalent screenshot blocking is unavailable on macOS and recommends excluding Signal from &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; there. The company is asking Apple, Google, and Microsoft for better tools to keep app content out of AI systems.<div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/signal/">Signal</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/24/signal-blocks-ai-access-to-protect-chats/">Signal Now Blocks AI Screen Access to Protect Chats</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/signal-now-blocks-ai-screen-access-to-protect-chats.2495142/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>